# Knowledge Hub Foundation Implementation Plan (Plan 1 of 4)

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** De-risk the two external unknowns (AssemblyAI EU, eve + Bedrock EU) and build `packages/knowledge` — the fully-tested data layer every later plan depends on.

**Architecture:** `packages/knowledge` is a source-only workspace package (like `@repo/database`, which it mirrors but never touches): Zod schemas are the single source of truth for six MongoDB collections, pure functions take a `Db` parameter for testability, and a `server-only` lazy singleton serves the apps. Spikes are throwaway scripts under `scripts/spikes/`.

**Tech Stack:** TypeScript 7 (strict), Zod ^4.4.3, mongodb ^7.5.0, Bun test, MongoDB Atlas (Frankfurt) in production / local `mongod` in tests.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-knowledge-hub-design.md`

## Global Constraints

- Package name `@repo/knowledge`, private, source-only (no build step), scripts `typecheck` + `test` + `clean` — mirroring `packages/database/package.json`.
- tsconfig extends `@repo/typescript-config/base.json`.
- Dependencies pinned to repo-wide versions: `zod` ^4.4.3, `mongodb` ^7.5.0, `@t3-oss/env-nextjs` ^0.13.11, `server-only` ^0.0.1; devDeps `@repo/typescript-config` workspace:*, `@types/node` 26.1.1, `typescript` ^7.0.2.
- `import "server-only"` ONLY in `client.ts`. Everything else must be importable from Bun tests (server-only throws outside React server environments).
- Every document carries `tenantId: string` (min 1). Tests use `"test-tenant"`.
- Integration tests read `MONGODB_TEST_URI` and skip when unset (`describe.skipIf`). Local runner: `docker run -d --name knowledge-test-mongo -p 27017:27017 mongo:8` → `MONGODB_TEST_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017`.
- EU-only endpoints: AssemblyAI `https://api.eu.assemblyai.com` exclusively; Bedrock region `eu-central-1` exclusively; Vercel AI Gateway is never used (no `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` anywhere).
- Do NOT modify `packages/database`.
- Before every commit: `bun run check` (ultracite/Biome) on the changed files; conventional commit messages (`feat:`, `chore:`, `test:`).
- Spike scripts and their result notes stay **untracked** (no commits) — they are throwaway; their outcomes are recorded as checkbox notes in this plan.

---

### Task 1: Spike A — AssemblyAI Universal-3.5 Pro on the EU endpoint

Verifies: the model runs on `api.eu.assemblyai.com`, German transcription quality is acceptable, and transcript deletion works. **Prerequisites:** an AssemblyAI account with a payment method (required for the training opt-out), `ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY` exported, and a short (~30s) German or German/English voice memo saved locally (record one on your phone; any format — m4a/mp3/wav).

**Files:**
- Create: `scripts/spikes/assemblyai-eu.ts` (untracked)

**Interfaces:**
- Produces: a go/no-go decision recorded in this plan. Later plans consume the confirmed request shape (`speech_models: ["universal-3-5-pro"]`, EU base URL).

- [ ] **Step 1: In the AssemblyAI dashboard, opt out of the Model Improvement Program** (Settings → Data Controls; Owner/Admin only). Do this before uploading any audio.

- [ ] **Step 2: Write the spike script**

```ts
// scripts/spikes/assemblyai-eu.ts
// Usage: ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=... bun scripts/spikes/assemblyai-eu.ts <path-to-audio>
const BASE_URL = "https://api.eu.assemblyai.com";
const apiKey = process.env.ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY;
const audioPath = process.argv[2];

if (!apiKey || !audioPath) {
  console.error("Usage: ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=... bun scripts/spikes/assemblyai-eu.ts <audio-file>");
  process.exit(1);
}

const headers = { authorization: apiKey };

// 1. Upload audio to the EU endpoint
const audio = await Bun.file(audioPath).arrayBuffer();
const uploadRes = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}/v2/upload`, {
  method: "POST",
  headers,
  body: audio,
});
if (!uploadRes.ok) {
  throw new Error(`Upload failed: ${uploadRes.status} ${await uploadRes.text()}`);
}
const { upload_url } = (await uploadRes.json()) as { upload_url: string };
console.log("Uploaded:", upload_url);

// 2. Request a transcript with Universal-3.5 Pro explicitly (no fallback),
//    so unavailability on EU surfaces as an error instead of silent downgrade.
const createRes = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}/v2/transcript`, {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { ...headers, "content-type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    audio_url: upload_url,
    speech_models: ["universal-3-5-pro"],
    language_detection: true,
  }),
});
if (!createRes.ok) {
  // If this 400s on the field name, check current docs: the parameter was
  // introduced as `speech_models` (array, ordered fallback).
  throw new Error(`Create failed: ${createRes.status} ${await createRes.text()}`);
}
const { id } = (await createRes.json()) as { id: string };
console.log("Transcript id:", id);

// 3. Poll until done
let transcript: { status: string; text?: string; speech_model_used?: string; error?: string };
do {
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 3000));
  const pollRes = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}/v2/transcript/${id}`, { headers });
  transcript = (await pollRes.json()) as typeof transcript;
  console.log("Status:", transcript.status);
} while (transcript.status === "queued" || transcript.status === "processing");

if (transcript.status === "error") {
  throw new Error(`Transcription failed: ${transcript.error}`);
}
console.log("speech_model_used:", transcript.speech_model_used);
console.log("---\n", transcript.text, "\n---");

// 4. Delete the transcript from AssemblyAI (the retention pattern we ship with)
const deleteRes = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}/v2/transcript/${id}`, {
  method: "DELETE",
  headers,
});
console.log("Delete:", deleteRes.status, deleteRes.ok ? "OK" : await deleteRes.text());
```

- [ ] **Step 3: Run it**

Run: `ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=<key> bun scripts/spikes/assemblyai-eu.ts ~/Downloads/testmemo.m4a`
Expected: status transitions to `completed`; `speech_model_used` prints `universal-3-5-pro`; German text is accurate (names, umlauts); delete returns 200.

- [ ] **Step 4: Record the outcome here**

Note in this checkbox: `speech_model_used` value, subjective German quality (usable / not), delete status. **Go/no-go:** if the model is unavailable on EU, note the error and we fall back to the default model array (`universal-2` fallback) or Deepgram EU — decide before Plan 2.

### Task 2: Spike B — eve `defineAgent` with a direct Bedrock `eu-central-1` model

Verifies the spec §5 spike: eve accepts a directly-configured AI SDK model instance, bypassing AI Gateway. **Prerequisites:** AWS account with Bedrock access, Claude model access granted in `eu-central-1` (AWS console → Bedrock → Model access), `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`/`AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` exported. AWS CLI configured (for the profile lookup).

**Files:**
- Create: `scripts/spikes/eve-bedrock/package.json`, `scripts/spikes/eve-bedrock/agent/agent.ts`, `scripts/spikes/eve-bedrock/agent/instructions.md` (all untracked)

**Interfaces:**
- Produces: architecture decision for Plan 4 — eve ask-agent (preferred) vs hand-rolled `streamText` loop (fallback).

- [ ] **Step 1: Find the current EU inference profile ID for Claude**

Run: `aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --region eu-central-1 --query "inferenceProfileSummaries[?contains(inferenceProfileId, 'claude')].inferenceProfileId"`
Expected: a list containing an `eu.anthropic.claude-...` profile (e.g. `eu.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0`). Use the newest Sonnet-class profile in the next step.

